{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-30T13:03:37.753Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7b0e58428f53e3aaeaafb372","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1626","claim:pm-gh1633","lineage:pm-gh1633","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1626+pm-gh1633","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1626","claim:pm-gh1633","lineage:pm-gh1633","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.312","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-30T13:03:37.753Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation evidence: the correction is now derived from runtime contracts rather than a hand list. resolveReadCompletenessControls joins each read-output surface's declared projection modes with the new CliFlagContract.values domain on --depth (get/context brief|standard|deep|full; plan brief|standard|deep). --<level> maps to --depth <level> only when the domain declares the level, --depth <level> maps to --<level> only for a declared projection mode, and --depth standard on a command without --depth replays without the flag. Aliased reads (deps, health) normalise to noun-first argv; the resolver maps item deps/ops health back to the read surface and replays on the canonical path. Same-command operands and globals are preserved. Conflicting --fields/--output-include/--section/--for or a second completeness flag, inline boolean values, and foreign commands get no retry. When no equivalent exists, for example search --depth brief, the refusal lists that command's own controls instead of pointing at other commands. Negative control, using a generated probe over every declaring surface (38 misspellings across 12 surfaces): the pre-fix build d9c4a0bca corrected 7/38; this build corrects 38/38 and every advertised retry executes with exit 0. One probe failure was its own spawnSync 1 MiB buffer on contracts --full, rerun with a larger buffer. Tests: 76 SDK cases generated from PM_READ_OUTPUT_SURFACE_CONTRACTS, plus a CLI integration test that executes one generated correction per surface and checks authoritative tracker bytes are unchanged. ESLint passes; contracts and SDK surface snapshots were updated, with the optional CliFlagContract.values acknowledged as a signature change."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-30T13:03:37.753Z"}],"before_hash":"70fad749d8db433a11f8c10e5a3af3e6c42af539543d8e7fe4f7fdc512275e37","after_hash":"9f1e3504ef8363894465c9df832c4c396f30fe3a32a991881c1fecfeae5c1a1f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"19dd7b78da7c345ad67a1e8a62c241d97422fa15c4b04c74b2f64259029478bc"}
